    DEFINITIONS

In this Agreement, the following terms have the following meanings:

Active: the Licensee shall be considered as Active regarding a
software when the Licensee has declared that it uses the software and
in particular has declared this either (i) through a direct or
indirect communication addressed to the Licensor or to the public, in
particular by means of an electronic mailing-list, of source code
managing systems or of "bug tracking" systems, and (ii) in any other
manner which logically makes the Licensor believe in a direct use by
the Licensee.

Commercial Use: any use of the software, other than research use,
notably the use of the software within a company.

Holder: the natural person who by not being in a situation of direct
competition with the initial Licensor creates modifications of the
software and communicates them to the initial Licensor so that they
are incorporated within the software.

Intellectual Property: all the elements of ownership concerning
industrial and intellectual property rights and in particular the
rights relating to software, inventions, utility models, industrial
designs, trade marks, get-up, trade names and domain names.

Initial Licensor: the natural or legal person that on the date of
this Agreement is designated as such and who has the authority to
grant licenses for software so designed and indicated as subject to
the provisions of this Agreement.

Licensor: the Initial Licensor and any other Holder who develops
modifications of the software under the provisions of Article 4.3.a
hereafter, who has accepted the provisions of this Agreement by
downloading or using the software or by expressly accepting this
Agreement in written form.

Licensee or User: any natural or legal person who uses the software
and in particular has the right to access and the right to use the
software in all its uses.

Modifications: all corrections, translations, adaptations, abridgements,
expansions, enhancements and any other alterations whatsoever of the
software, and any incorporation in the software of any software,
routine or function developed by the Licensee.

Module: a set of sources files including their documentation that
permits to implement a set of functions or services in addition or
different when this set and its associated documentation constitute a
functional entity which can be independently used and re-utilized.

Object code: the binary-form code resulting from the translation and
any processing whatsoever of Source code.

Source code: all the software's instructions and data files in their
source state, including all the intermediate results of such processing.

The Software: the software in Object code and/or Source code form,
being either an initial version indicated in the header or any other
version indicated in the header and more generally any software program
contained in this Agreement.

These expressions may be used in either singular or plural form.

    ARTICLE 1 : OBJECT

The aim of this Free Software license agreement is to grant users the
right to use the Software in the widest sense of the word, as described
below:

1. Right of use: The Licensee is authorized to use the Software in any
use, including commercial use, subject in all cases to the provisions
of this Agreement.

2. Right of study, modification and adaptation: The Licensee is
authorized to study, modify, adapt the Software provided that he/she
fully discloses modifications, under the conditions set out below:

    The Licensee undertakes to disclose and communicate
    modifications made to the software to the Initial Licensor within
    thirty days from the date of completion.

3. Right of representation, diffusion and diffusion of modifications:

   The Licensee is authorized to represent, sell, lease, rent,
   disclose, transmit or generally distribute the Software, as object
   code and/or source code, but only under the following conditions:

   The Licensee shall systematically disclose to the Licensor the
   source code of any object code he distributes and inform the
   Licensor that this software is distributed under the CeCILL
   license. The Licensee undertakes to leave intact all copyright
   notices on the software.

   The Licensee shall systematically disclose to end-users the source
   code of the distributed software.

    ARTICLE 2: ACCEPTATION

2.1 Full acceptation of the entire Agreement.

Each Licensee acknowledges having read, and accepted the full
provisions of this Agreement.

2.2 Form of such acceptance.

Such acceptance may be done (i) by implementing the obligation of
Article 4.1 hereafter if this is the first Commercial Use of the
Software by the Licensee or (ii) by implementing the obligation of
Article 4.3.b hereafter if the Licensee modifies the Software or
(iii) by simply using the Software and in any case before any
Commercial Use.

    ARTICLE 3: EFFECTIVE DATE

This Agreement shall become effective on the date when the Licensee
uses the Software in any manner whatsoever.

    ARTICLE 4: RIGHTS AND OBLIGATIONS OF LICENSEES

4.1. In the case of use for scientific purposes:

a) The Licensee undertakes, according to the means and capacities
which are his, to ensure continuity of the development of the Software.
To this end the Licensee will communicate to the Licensor all
improvements and modifications he makes to the Software. The Licensor
will have the right to use freely these improvements and modifications.

b) The Licensee undertakes to acknowledge the contribution of the
Licensor in publications or communications having as their principal
subject to describe functions or improvements of the Software. The
Licensee commits himself at least to mention the name of the Licensor.

4.2. Obligations specific to Commercial Use:

If the Licensee makes commercial use of the Software, the Licensee
agrees to inform the Initial Licensor in writing of this commercial
use before the first commercial distribution.

4.3. Obligations in the case of modification:

a) In any case, the Licensee who modifies the Software shall permit
the Licensor to incorporate his modifications within the Software
unless he/she has accepted the provisions of clause 4.3.b below.

b) The Licensee shall give the Initial Licensor the possibility within
a period of three months to incorporate his/her modifications within
the Software. It is reminded that the Initial Licensor has the right to
refuse the incorporation of any modifications which it considers not
appropriate according to its right of evaluation.

c) If the Licensor refuses the incorporation of modifications, the
Licensor shall provide detailed written reasons which will form an
integral part of the dispute.

d) If the Initial Licensor refuses the incorporation of modifications,
the Licensee shall then have the right to use his modified version of
the Software under the conditions set out in Article 1.

e) The Licensee may, in any case, distribute the modified version
under the CeCILL license subject to the obligation to disclose the
source code to end-users and to inform them clearly and in a visible
manner that the Software has been modified, specifying on which date
these modifications have been made. The Licensee undertakes to cause
the modified Software to be governed by this Agreement.

4.4 Obligations as regards Passive Licensees:

Each Licensee shall be an Active Licensee in relation to the Initial
Licensor as soon as the Licensee makes a commercial use of the Software.
The Initial Licensor may consider as a Passive Licensee any Licensee who
does not communicate any improvement on the Software or does not make a
declaration of commercial use within thirty days of the date when this
Licensee was identified.

