    ARTICLE 8: TERMINATION

8.1 Termination of this Agreement may be pronounced on the initiative of
the Licensor.

8.2 The Licensor may, in the event of breach of the provisions of this
Agreement by the Licensee, suspend the Licensee from the right to use the
Software after a formal notice, sent by electronic mail to the last address
of the Licensee if this one is available, thirty days after the date of
said notice. If the Licensee has not regularized his situation before the
expiration of this period of thirty days, the Licensor may terminate this
Agreement and the associated license.

8.3 In the event of termination of the Agreement as provided for in Article
8.2, the termination shall not affect the rights granted to end-users under
the present Agreement, as long as they comply with the conditions of the
present Agreement.

    ARTICLE 9: MISCELLANEOUS

9.1 Severability. If any provision of this Agreement is held to be invalid
or unenforceable for any reason, the validity and enforceability of the
remaining provisions shall not be affected.

9.2 Entire Agreement. This Agreement constitutes the entire agreement
relating to the use of the Software.

Any other prior agreement, whether written or oral, relating to the use of
the Software is superseded hereby. In the event of any conflict between the
provisions of this Agreement and any other document, the terms of this
Agreement shall govern.

9.3 French language. The original Agreement has been written in French and
translated into English. In case of conflict or for an authoritative
interpretation, reference is made to the French version. Licensees may
request a translation into any language and agree to the fact that the
Initial Licensor may use the translation as reference for interpreting the
Agreement.

9.4 Governing Law and Jurisdiction. This Agreement shall be governed by
French law. Any litigation relating to the provisions of this Agreement
shall be subject to the jurisdiction of the Tribunal de Grande Instance
de Paris.

